    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26066" root="ضنأ" body-key="D">
    
      8 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضْطَنَأَ لَهُ</span></b>  and 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْهُ</span></b>  <i>He was abashed at,</i> or
<i>shy of,</i> and <i>he shrank at,</i> or <i>from, him,</i> or <i>it.</i>
(M, K. [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضطبأ</span>.]) Et-Tirimmáh uses
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِضْطَنَا</span> [or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِضْطَنَى</span> in this sense,] and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يَضْطَنِى</span>:
meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اضطنأ</span> [and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يضطنئ</span>]: or as being derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الضَّنَى</span> meaning “ disease. ” (M.)

